+    /* THE LINE LAW: a word longer than its line (a file name, a URL, an id) breaks
+       where the line ends instead of pushing the part past its container, where a
+       scroller above it then pans sideways or a plate's `overflow: hidden` cuts it off.
+
+       The surfaces that hold prose, and the Label, break such a word only where it
+       would overflow: `break-word` leaves every intrinsic size alone, so a short word
+       in a narrow cell never splits.
+
+       The rows a plate gives its width to (menu and Command rows, the Accordion
+       trigger, the Select trigger) also give the word up in their min-content
+       (`anywhere`): the label is a flex item, and a flex item cannot shrink below a
+       word that will not break. Their width comes from outside, so the label gives up
+       only a word wider than the whole row, and the Select trigger's one-line value
+       (`line-clamp-1`) ends in its ellipsis. The rest of the row inherits `anywhere`
+       too: a shortcut opts out below, and a Badge keeps its one line (`nowrap`).
+
+       Buttons, Chips, toggle items and badges keep every word whole. They size to
+       their own label, and with `anywhere` a table column or a squeezed row could
+       narrow them to a letter a line. */
